		(uuid "b90b2865-c25a-49ad-b793-9d9fefafe1aa")
	)
	(text "Forward current datasheet: max 1000mA, \nmeaning max brightness \noccurs when forward current = 1000mA\nForward current chosen for safety/thermal \nconsiderations (LEDs get hot) = 500mA\nForward voltage datasheet: 2.7V-3.6V\n\nFormula 1)\nSupply voltage >= LED forward voltage + \nvoltage needed by current-limiting resistor\nSo we set supply voltage at 4V, not 3V3, \nbecause max forward voltage is 3.6V. \nThat leaves 0.4V for resistor. \n\nFormula 2)\nR=(V supply - V forward)/I forward\n\nTwo cases for R:\n1. Rmin = (4V-3.6V)/500mA\nRmin= 0.8 ohms\n\n2. Rmax=(4V-2.7V)/500mA\nRmax= 2.6 ohms\n\nIf we want max current to be 500mA, we need \nto be <=500mA. Current is max \nwhen Vf= 2.7V. So we choose R=2.6 ohms "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 216.408 61.468 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b9d40d01-4c63-4a90-a3b9-1fb7038a522c")
	)
	(text "Why 4V supply voltage :\n\nForward voltage datasheet: 2.7V-3.6V\n\nFormula 1)\nSupply voltage >= LED forward voltage + voltage needed by \ncurrent-limiting (drain) resistor\nSo we set supply voltage at 4V, not 3V3, \nbecause max forward voltage is 3.6V. That leaves 0.4V for resistor. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 216.408 101.092 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "eb1f223e-10d0-4eb6-a8b1-74707292b968")
	)
	(text "Calculate power dissipation P=I^2R\n\nFor R28, R29, dissipation power is the same\nP= (0.5A)^2*10 ohms\nP=2.5W for each"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 91.44 167.386 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fab69f65-52d9-4dd5-b2ce-cde5320ec54f")
	)
